Enable kdump and vmcore capture on Wistron ARM64 platforms.

1. Build makedumpfile with ARM64 52-bit VA support for 4K-page kernels
   using fixed upstream commit cecce00ab4f3, with epoch 1 and apt hold.
2. Configure kdump-tools cmdline: remove irqpoll, add reset_devices, and
   set systemd.unit=kdump-tools-dump.service on ARM64 platforms.
3. Update default KDUMP memory in init_cfg.json.j2 to
   0M-2G:0M,2G-64G:512M,64G-:512M.

